<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    A-026 non-Unity player package — the C# half of the two-process client.

    This is the SAME verified build shape as harness.csproj, not a new guess:
    EnableDefaultCompileItems must be false (default true plus an explicit
    <Compile> is NETSDK1022 "Duplicate 'Compile' items", a build failure),
    globs resolve relative to the CS PROJ (repo root), and with default items
    off the <Compile> element's Exclude ATTRIBUTE works while an <Exclude>
    ELEMENT is inert.

    Why the harness files are in this build: Commands.emitSnapshot is the ONE
    snapshot emitter in the repo, and the payload-vs-snapshot acceptance
    criterion is byte-exact by construction only if the player embeds THAT
    emitter's output. Re-implementing it here would be a second emitter, which
    A-019 forbids.

    Why tools/harness/main.cs is excluded: it owns HarnessEntry.Main, the fork
    guard, and forkExpected. The player supplies its own entry point
    (SimHost.Main), and two entry points in one target is a link error. No
    other harness file references those symbols (probed by grep), so excluding
    it cannot break the build; if that ever stopped being true the build would
    fail loudly, not pass quietly.

    The three contract-only Unity stubs are excluded exactly as in the harness
    target. The exclusion is provably real, not vacuous: RenderLayer.cs and
    UIRoot.cs reference UnityEngine.* which does not exist in this toolchain,
    so a broken Exclude yields CS0234/CS0103 rather than a quiet pass.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="Assets/**/*.cs"
             Exclude="Assets/Runtime/Bridge/Unity/GameLoop.cs;Assets/Runtime/Bridge/Unity/RenderLayer.cs;Assets/Runtime/Bridge/Unity/UIRoot.cs;Assets/Editor/BuildPlayerPackage.cs" />
    <Compile Include="tools/harness/*.cs"
             Exclude="tools/harness/main.cs" />
    <Compile Include="tools/player/SimHost.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
